WEBVTT

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:04.210
Everyone, Kaleido Star is about to start!

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:06.980
When watching Kaleido Star,
please keep the room brightly lit,

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.670
and sit as far from the TV as you can.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:14.850
I'm Sora Naegino.
I came to America all by myself

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:16.420
with aspirations of joining Kaleido Stage.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.150
Everything is new to me,

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.620
but I'm doing my best in the spirit of
"try it rather than think about it."

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.060
There's nothing I can't do if I try

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.830
and if I can do it without trying,
I'd be super lucky.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.890
And if I'm gonna do it, I just gotta do it!
Gotta! Gotta! That's me.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.500
Well, well, well, what's your father like?

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.370
Is he nice or is he scary?

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:41.640
Miss Layla's father is a workaholic
and he has no clue about her feelings.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.410
Even on her special birthday, he's working.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.080
Oh! If he keeps acting that way,
I feel sorry for Miss Layla!

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.610
I do! I do!

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:06.190
<i>Yaritai koto wa nani</i>

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:06.190
<i>What is it that you want to do?</i>

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:09.830
<i>Sou kikareru tabi</i>

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:09.830
<i>Every time I was asked that</i>

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:13.560
<i>Aoi sora miageta</i>

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:13.560
<i>I looked up at the blue sky</i>

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.580
<i>Kotae wa only my heart</i>

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.580
<i>The answer is only in my heart</i>

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:25.120
<i>Honto ni daiji na kotoba wa
kantan ni wa iwanai</i>

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:25.120
<i>I don't easily say the words
that are really important</i>

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:32.390
<i>Hikari ga yubisasu basho e to hashiridasu yo</i>

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:32.390
<i>I start running towards the place
the light points to</i>

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:40.370
<i>Dakishimetai mono nara
nakitai hodo mune ni aru</i>

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:40.370
<i>There's so much in my heart that I want
to embrace, I could cry</i>

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:47.310
<i>Egakitsuzukete yuku kitto
take it someday</i>

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:47.310
<i>I'll keep painting my way, I promise,
take it someday</i>

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:55.280
<i>Shiroi kumo ga nagareru
chiheisen no mukou ni</i>

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:55.280
<i>Beyond the horizon, where
the white clouds drift</i>

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:07.060
<i>Naranderu mirai wa itsumo soba ni aru kara</i>

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:07.060
<i>The future is lined up and
it'll always be there by my side</i>

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:29.020
Can I do a grieving chimpanzee pose
at the end today?

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:30.080
No.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:34.250
Oh, sorry.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:35.890
My chance!

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:38.150
I should say something to make them laugh!

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:40.230
As you may expect from roses!

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:42.960
Roses...

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.330
Oh! Darn it!

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.160
I wish I could be better at ad-libing.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.640
That look is perfect!

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:55.110
Anyway, that's a big bouquet.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:56.540
I know. It's for Miss Layla.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:59.110
Her father, Mr. Hamilton, is here.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.280
Oh? Does he come here often?

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.990
Well, he's very busy, so he's rarely here.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:06.590
He's the owner of Hamilton Hotels.

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:08.120
Hamilton Hotels?

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.920
I think we have some in Japan too.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:11.860
They're all over the world.

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.260
Wow...

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.460
Oh, I need to deliver this quick.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:17.590
He sounds great.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:19.900
An Amazing Star Even In Tough Times

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:22.800
An Amazing Star Even In Tough Times

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:22.800
"An Amazing Star Even In Tough Times"

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:25.640
An Amazing Star Even In Tough Times

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:29.680
It seems like "Cinderella" will be
one of Layla's best works.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.950
How is the box-office record?

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:34.620
The audience numbers are
the best in history.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:37.240
Who are these three fairy godmothers?

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.590
They're new-comers who passed
the audition this year.

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:40.650
I see.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:42.460
Father.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:43.760
Ah, Layla.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:45.860
Congratulations on the
successful production.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:46.790
Thank you.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.830
Also, thank you for the beautiful flowers too.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:51.820
There is no flower that exceeds
your beauty, Layla.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:55.470
I really would like you
to see my show this time.

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:56.900
I don't have the time.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:00.740
By the way, we're having a party with
the top business leaders tonight.

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:02.910
Make sure you come to the party
after your show.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:04.750
I will.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:06.580
Kalos, please be her escort.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.210
Yes, I will.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:11.710
And let's invite those three fairy
godmothers too.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.550
Those three?

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:15.290
It's important to provide them with publicity.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.590
We need to have the next generation
of stars after you leave.

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:21.320
Then, I will see you tonight, Layla.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.100
He is such a busy person.

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:34.800
Yes. So busy that he has never seen one
of my shows to the end.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:39.310
We did it perfectly again today.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:43.650
The audience seemed like they were
waiting for the transformation scene,

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.220
so it's really worth doing, you know?

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:48.020
Why don't we stumble off the stage
when we exit next time?

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.290
No way.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:50.630
I agree.

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:51.850
That's what I figured.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:57.530
Just because you're a little popular,

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.190
don't give an unfocused performance!

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:01.840
We're sorry.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.210
But we were perfect today.

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:07.840
Our top star is in a bad mood.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.840
Maybe she's more uptight than usual

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.250
because her father's here
to see her performance.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:14.280
But I think he left without watching the show.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:14.810
What?

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:16.910
I didn't know.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:19.320
All of you,

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.450
go to the costume department.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:24.890
A party?!

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.000
It's kind of awkward.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.490
I wonder if I should say something?

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:38.610
It was too bad that your father couldn't
stay for your show today.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:39.700
That's nothing new.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:42.980
Oh, really?

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:44.810
This is awkward.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:56.320
So beautiful.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:58.030
It's Layla Hamilton.

00:05:58.030 --> 00:05:59.290
She is stunning.

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:01.190
You look beautiful, Layla.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:03.220
Thank you, Father.

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:06.770
Hey, Sora.

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:07.760
What's wrong?

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:11.330
Somehow, I feel like I don't belong here.

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:14.380
No, I'll be all right.

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:15.240
Hello...

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:17.880
It's definitely more nerve-racking
than performing on stage.

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.180
That's true.

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:22.080
It seems like they're drawing attention.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:22.920
Yes.

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.990
By the way, do you know that man?

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:26.490
He looks familiar.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:28.460
If I remember correctly,
he's a movie producer.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:29.490
That's right.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:32.190
He's looking for a heroine for his next movie.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:34.790
Audition for the role.

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:39.120
Miss Layla is going to audition for a movie?

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.140
This is a great opportunity.

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:43.970
To advance your career from being
Kaleido Stage's top star

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:45.510
to becoming a worldwide top star.

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:48.370
You have that much commercial value.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:51.870
I understand.

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:53.380
Miss Layla.

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:54.680
Miss Layla!

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.580
I saw you in the newspaper.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:58.450
Aren't you that fairy godmother?

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:00.220
You're so cute.

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:02.690
Hey, how do you do that Triple Illusion?

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:04.490
Do something for us.

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:06.860
Yes! Please show us.

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:08.900
What should we do?

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.000
You want to do something?

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.430
Let's put on a little show.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:12.030
What?

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.600
Sora, let's do it.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:14.570
Yeah!

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:18.210
Here!

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:20.840
There, there, there, there, there, there!

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:34.950
Tada!

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:38.230
It's them.

00:07:38.230 --> 00:07:38.830
Here, Sora!

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:39.880
Here!

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:47.530
Tada!

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:52.810
Well, well, not bad.

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:55.170
If you would come to the actual stage,
you could...

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:58.410
Thank you, thank you.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.310
Please come see Kaleido Stage.

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:02.450
Now, for a little party joke.

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:03.310
Ladies.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:06.390
Oh, Miss Layla's father.

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:08.180
I have a favor to ask.

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:09.660
Yes?

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:12.550
To tell you the truth, tomorrow is
Layla's birthday.

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:15.160
We're having a party at our house
in the afternoon.

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:17.370
Won't you three come to the party too?

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:18.470
Really?

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:19.500
Definitely!

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:20.500
Oh, I know!

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:22.500
If you have the day off tomorrow,

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:25.300
please come and watch our show
after the party.

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:28.800
I have to work tomorrow.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:31.450
I will make sure you get paid for your work.

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:33.140
So please be there.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:36.280
Please, wait.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:37.810
What?

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:39.790
We don't need to be paid.

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:42.690
We'll still go even if we're not paid.

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:44.230
You certainly are generous.

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:46.490
You will never be successful like that.

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:50.100
He's awful.

00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:54.970
That's nothing new.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:58.490
I wonder if Miss Layla is lonely?

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:13.020
So, I think we should brighten up the
mood at the party tomorrow.

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:14.220
Oh...

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:16.090
That's what I'm thinking...

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:16.990
Oh!

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:17.960
What?

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:20.550
Oh, nothing...

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:23.700
What?!

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:24.930
Cancelled?

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:26.670
Yes, it was cancelled.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:27.970
What's going on?

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:30.900
Can we at least give her a present?

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.200
What's going on?

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:35.740
What are you all doing?

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:37.770
Well, Miss Layla...

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:40.240
Happy birthday!

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:43.010
Thank you.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:44.590
You're welcome.

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:46.210
My father asked you to come, didn't he?

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:47.150
Yes.

00:09:47.150 --> 00:09:48.160
Excuse me,

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:49.920
but why was it suddenly cancelled?

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:51.590
It wasn't sudden.

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:57.290
Every year, my father invites guests
to the party by paying them.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:00.100
But a party like that is meaningless.

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:03.290
I suppose so.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:06.840
That's why I cancel it every year.

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:12.780
It sounds like your father doesn't
understand your feelings at all.

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:14.820
That's how things work here.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:20.010
But even so, he cares about me
in his own way.

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:21.550
That's enough for me.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:24.090
Well, haven't you heard enough?

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:25.560
Please go home.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:26.550
Okay.

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.890
I have to practice now.

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:30.630
Practice?

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:31.890
At home?

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.170
Wow...

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:37.230
Amazing.

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:40.370
I can't believe there's a practice room
inside the house.

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:43.940
How often do you practice here, Miss Layla?

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:47.650
Unless I have practice for a
new production, everyday.

00:10:47.650 --> 00:10:49.780
And on the days when my performance
was unsatisfactory on stage.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:51.490
That often?

00:10:51.490 --> 00:10:52.680
It's your birthday today and you're still...

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:58.460
Someday, I want my father to
acknowledge Kaleido Stage.

00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:03.220
And for that, my performance
has to be the best at all times.

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:05.090
Miss Layla...

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:08.000
The movie audition, maybe you're actually...

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:09.770
I will audition for the movie.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.870
I'll make sure to live up to his expectations.

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:15.310
Because I don't want to disappoint him.

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:19.050
Aren't you satisfied now?

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:19.940
Please leave.

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:22.880
Okay, thank you.

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:45.700
All right, I've decided!

00:11:46.570 --> 00:11:47.470
Decided what?

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:02.920
Then after the curtain drops,

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:05.930
the curtain call will become
Miss Layla's birthday party!

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:07.730
Doesn't it sound like magic?

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:09.930
Once we've decided to do this, let's hurry!

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:10.970
Mia is the director.

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:12.900
Ken and Jean are in charge of the stage sets.

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:16.270
And Anna and Miss Sarah,
please make the costumes.

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:17.970
Oh, Marion, you need to help us, too.

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:20.540
Since we don't have much time left
before the evening show,

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:21.670
let's get started now.

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:24.040
Huh?

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:25.450
What are you all doing?

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:26.940
Hurry, hurry!

00:12:28.650 --> 00:12:31.080
Once she makes up her mind,
she's the type that runs with it.

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:33.420
That's one of her good traits.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:34.560
I couldn't agree more.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:36.960
Is there any sort of trick to this?

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:38.790
Just do an adequate job, I guess.

00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:40.190
Oh...

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:42.230
What is this? It's fun!

00:12:42.230 --> 00:12:43.360
Marion!

00:12:46.270 --> 00:12:46.900
Ready?

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:47.890
Yes.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:52.640
I wonder how she'll react?

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:54.710
I can't wait.

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:56.310
Are you up to something again?

00:12:56.310 --> 00:12:59.610
Oh, we're going to celebrate
Miss Layla's birthday.

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:01.580
But please keep it a secret.

00:13:01.850 --> 00:13:03.450
I hope everything turns out well.

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:05.380
Yes! Thank you.

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:12.020
Okay? Jonathan, you're going to hand the
cake to Miss Layla at the end.

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:18.900
All right.

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.900
Now, everything is all set to go.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:22.030
No, not yet.

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:26.000
Without this, it won't be magic.

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:29.410
Are you serious?

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:30.410
Of course.

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:32.910
Even if you want it, that's impossible.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:34.720
You can't contact him?

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:38.240
Well, I can contact him, but...

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:39.710
You can't?

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:43.890
I guess we can't do it after all.

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:45.260
Oh, fine!

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:46.730
It's time to sink or swim!

00:13:46.730 --> 00:13:48.300
Oh, then...

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:50.630
Yeah, I'll try to contact him.

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:51.830
Thank you!

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:57.440
Yes. Mr. Hamilton please. Yes.

00:13:57.440 --> 00:14:00.100
She needs to talk to him
concerning Miss Layla.

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:03.900
Her name is Sora Naegino,
from Kaleido Stage.

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:06.910
Oh, well, she's still new.

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:08.620
I'm not suspicious or anything.

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:10.020
I am a fairy godmother!

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:11.220
What?!

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:13.150
That sounds plenty suspicious.

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:13.910
No way!

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:20.350
Mr. Hamilton, you have a phone call.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:21.720
I'm in the middle of a meeting.

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:23.150
But...

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:26.760
It's from someone called "fairy godmother."

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:30.100
Shall I contact the police?

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:31.330
No, I'll take it.

00:14:32.210 --> 00:14:34.300
I'm sorry to call you at work.

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:36.640
So, what business does a
fairy godmother have with me?

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:39.250
Do you want to get paid
for the party after all?

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:40.680
The party was cancelled.

00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:41.380
What?

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:42.910
It has been cancelled every year.

00:14:43.350 --> 00:14:46.080
Miss Layla was practicing by herself.

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:47.920
That's ridiculous.

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:51.360
We're having a birthday party for her
at Kaleido Stage.

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:55.160
And we would very much like you
to attend the party.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.200
That's impossible.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:58.630
Even if it's impossible, please!

00:14:58.630 --> 00:15:01.540
Actually, I want you to see
Miss Layla's show, but...

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:05.130
It takes four hours from here to
Cape Mary even by private jet.

00:15:05.610 --> 00:15:07.310
I won't make it in time for the
start of the show.

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:10.340
Then at least, can you make it to the
end of the show? Please!

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:11.850
Thank you for letting me know.

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:14.040
Thanks to you, I now know how Layla feels.

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:18.810
Looks like she wasn't happy with
a party that I bought for her.

00:15:19.990 --> 00:15:21.520
You still don't get it.

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:22.490
What?

00:15:22.760 --> 00:15:26.060
You don't understand how Miss Layla feels.

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:29.160
It doesn't matter how many people are there.

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:31.530
If the person she wants most to be there
doesn't come,

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:33.500
she'll just feel even more alone.

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:35.740
She feels lonely and sad.

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:39.830
I think that's why she cancels the
parties and just practices by herself.

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:43.010
She needs her father.

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:44.500
So, please.

00:15:45.780 --> 00:15:47.040
Please come.

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:51.650
Inviting Miss Layla's father?

00:15:51.650 --> 00:15:54.050
Yes. It seems Sora is calling him right now.

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:55.390
That's impossible.

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:57.880
You never know, because it's Sora.

00:15:59.630 --> 00:16:00.460
Come in.

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:01.960
Excuse us.

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:02.930
What is it?

00:16:02.930 --> 00:16:07.470
Miss Layla, your father's like,
coming to see your show.

00:16:07.470 --> 00:16:09.600
My father? There is no way.

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:12.390
But today's your birthday, so...

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:11.930
What's going on?

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:35.480
Happy birthday, Layla!

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:41.190
Happy birthday, Miss Layla!

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:43.090
Sora...

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:45.130
This is from all of us.

00:17:45.470 --> 00:17:46.770
A small...

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:48.030
present.

00:17:53.310 --> 00:17:54.370
That's impossible.

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:22.990
All right!

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:35.450
Yeah! It was a big success!

00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:36.850
We did it, Sora!

00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:38.290
Yeah, I'm so glad.

00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:39.980
Miss Layla seemed happy with...

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:43.210
What is the meaning of this?

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:45.010
Did you come up with this?!

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:48.300
Yes.

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:49.520
Stop doing things like this!

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:53.430
I've never appeared so dumbstruck
in front of an audience before.

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:56.770
Oh... I'm sorry.

00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:59.500
Please don't do anything like this again.

00:19:01.710 --> 00:19:03.230
Excuse me, Miss Layla.

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:04.480
What?

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:05.570
You still have something?

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:07.610
At the very least, please take this cake.

00:19:07.610 --> 00:19:10.280
Well, the cake isn't really that important,

00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:11.650
but there's a message.

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:15.360
I got this message personally
from your father.

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:16.380
What?

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:19.180
That's all right.

00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:24.260
I thought everything turned out fine.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:25.990
Don't be discouraged, Sora.

00:19:26.270 --> 00:19:28.070
It's not your fault.

00:19:28.070 --> 00:19:29.440
It's your fault.

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:32.270
I knew it. It was like, unnecessary after all.

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:49.320
I got this message personally
from your father.

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:52.660
Please don't do anything like this again.

00:19:56.200 --> 00:19:59.100
Why am I so irritated?

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:02.530
Happy birthday, Miss Layla.

00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:23.820
It's because I pushed for the birthday party.

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:26.160
No, we were all in on it.

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:28.990
I guess Miss Layla doesn't like
that sort of thing.

00:20:29.230 --> 00:20:35.400
In the end, I ignored Miss Layla's
feelings just like her father did.

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:37.270
What should we do with that cake?

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:38.170
You want to eat it?

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:40.430
Well, we did take the time to make it.

00:20:40.970 --> 00:20:41.940
Yeah.

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:47.250
I'm going to at least
deliver the message to her.

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:48.280
Sora.

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:50.120
She may get mad at you again.

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:52.880
Well, I'm already used to
someone being mad at me.

00:20:54.050 --> 00:20:56.020
Sora, I'm coming in!

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:57.190
Please do!

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:59.030
Oh, here it is! Here it is.

00:20:59.030 --> 00:21:00.490
I'm so glad.

00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:02.160
What is it?

00:21:02.460 --> 00:21:06.500
Miss Layla's maid just came
to pick up the cake.

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:07.430
What?

00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:10.400
She said she'll at least accept the cake
since you took the time to make it.

00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:11.940
Really!

00:21:11.940 --> 00:21:14.000
Layla can be so pretentious sometimes.

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:17.780
Then, I will leave the cake here.

00:21:17.780 --> 00:21:18.840
Excuse me.

00:21:31.730 --> 00:21:32.820
Fax?

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:41.760
Happy birthday, Layla.

00:21:42.300 --> 00:21:45.170
You're always sparkling in my heart.

00:21:45.440 --> 00:21:47.370
My Kaleido Star.

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:54.610
It's so difficult somehow.

00:21:55.980 --> 00:21:59.980
I guess even real families worry about
their opinions of each other.

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:02.160
I wonder if that's the way everyone acts?

00:22:02.160 --> 00:22:03.620
I think that it is.

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:05.580
I see.

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:09.430
Won't you worry about my opinions
once in a while too?

00:22:09.430 --> 00:22:10.430
No, I will not.

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:11.400
Wha...

00:22:13.030 --> 00:22:15.520
Happy birthday, Miss Layla.

00:22:22.340 --> 00:22:24.950
<i>When you sabishii toki doushitemasuka</i>

00:22:22.340 --> 00:22:24.950
<i>When you're lonely, what do you do?</i>

00:22:24.950 --> 00:22:27.350
<i>Never say sonna no wakannai</i>

00:22:24.950 --> 00:22:27.350
<i>Never say you don't get any of that</i>

00:22:27.350 --> 00:22:30.250
<i>Nemuru asobu magazine mekuru</i>

00:22:27.350 --> 00:22:30.250
<i>Sleep, play, flip through a magazine</i>

00:22:30.250 --> 00:22:32.590
<i>Sabishii toki wa sabishii yo</i>

00:22:30.250 --> 00:22:32.590
<i>When you're lonely, you're lonely</i>

00:22:32.590 --> 00:22:37.360
<i>Mienai denpa ga kyou mo
tulututu machi ni tobikau</i>

00:22:32.590 --> 00:22:37.360
<i>Like always, invisible vibes fly around
the city today, tulututu</i>

00:22:37.360 --> 00:22:42.030
<i>Anyway kokoro no bekutoru
so many reason hanashiteru</i>

00:22:37.360 --> 00:22:42.030
<i>Anyway, the vector of my heart is
talking about so many reasons</i>

00:22:42.030 --> 00:22:46.700
<i>Jiyuu ni sora o tobitai keredo</i>

00:22:42.030 --> 00:22:46.700
<i>I want to be free and fly the skies</i>

00:22:46.700 --> 00:22:51.410
<i>Hane o hirogeru basho ga nai</i>

00:22:46.700 --> 00:22:51.410
<i>But I don't have space to spread my wings</i>

00:22:51.410 --> 00:22:53.570
<i>Demo shinjiteru</i>

00:22:51.410 --> 00:22:53.570
<i>But I have faith</i>

00:22:53.570 --> 00:22:58.250
<i>Katachi no nai mirai ga aru yo</i>

00:22:53.570 --> 00:22:58.250
<i>There is a future yet to be shaped</i>

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:02.950
<i>Katachi ni shitai watashi ga iru</i>

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:02.950
<i>And there's a me that I want to shape</i>

00:23:02.950 --> 00:23:09.390
<i>Kanashikutemo machigai demo</i>

00:23:02.950 --> 00:23:09.390
<i>Even if I'm sad, even if it's a mistake</i>

00:23:09.390 --> 00:23:14.760
<i>Omou mama fly to the free</i>

00:23:09.390 --> 00:23:14.760
<i>I'll do what I want and
fly towards the freedom</i>

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:22.530
Next Kaleido Star

00:23:22.940 --> 00:23:25.870
Don't you have any stars other than Layla?

00:23:25.870 --> 00:23:28.810
And so, for the heroine of the
upcoming production, "The Little Mermaid,"

00:23:28.810 --> 00:23:31.340
I end up auditioning in front of an
important person without rehearsal!

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:32.580
But Sora makes a mistake.

00:23:32.580 --> 00:23:34.050
She becomes afraid and unable to jump.

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:36.110
Don't worry, Sora. Trust me.

00:23:37.120 --> 00:23:40.590
What's gonna happen to me? What? What?

00:23:40.590 --> 00:23:43.290
Next time on Kaleido Star,
"My Amazing Challenge For the Lead Role"

